infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title The transaction-id age ladder to the 2-billion wall
  desc One finite 32-bit budget — Postgres enforces the top rung for you by refusing connections
  order asc
  sequences
    - label 200M — VACUUM freezes (autovacuum_freeze_max_age)
      desc Tuples older than this get t_xmin rewritten to FrozenTransactionId. Anti-wraparound freeze runs even when autovacuum = off.
    - label 1B — alert on age(datfrozenxid)
      desc First operational threshold. Freezing is falling behind; investigate autovacuum throughput before it compounds.
    - label 1.5B — page the on-call
      desc Margin is thin. At this rate you risk reaching the shutdown wall; escalate and consider manual freezing.
    - label ~2B — Postgres refuses commands
      desc "database is not accepting commands to avoid wraparound data loss" — emergency single-user freeze only. Sentry 2017.
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e #8b5cf6
